`;r||await e.writeFile("/guidelines/setup.md",'## Step 1: Install css\n\nAdd this line to the TOP of `/src/styles/index.css` (before any other imports):\n\n```css\n@import "<PACKAGE_NAME>/style.css";\n```\n\nThis import defines all CSS custom properties (color tokens, spacing tokens,\nradius tokens) used by this design system. Without it, var(--token-name)\nreferences will resolve to nothing and the UI will have no styling.\n\n## Step 2: Read the full design system stylesheet\n\nAfter importing, read the full contents of the stylesheet to understand what\ntokens are available:\n\n```\ncat node_modules/<PACKAGE_NAME>/dist/style.css\n```\n\nDo NOT use `head -100` or any truncated read. The file begins with Tailwind\npreflight/reset CSS (box-sizing, margins, etc.) which is NOT the design system.\nThe actual token definitions (CSS custom properties like `--text-default`,\n`--bg-brand`, `--spacer-*`, etc.) appear AFTER the preflight section.\n\nScan the full output for `:root` or `@theme` blocks containing `--` custom\nproperty definitions. These are the tokens you must use in generated code.\n'),await e.writeFile(eH.dY,a)}var e3=r(606181),e6=r(253329),e4=r(624058),e8=r(621325);let e7="{{SETUP_DIFF}}",e9=`Your job is to examine the project setup and produce a setup guideline document that an AI code-generation agent can later use to correctly configure new projects to use this design system.

## Input

${e7}

The npm package list and agent constraints have been pre-written to \`/guidelines/setup.md\`. Read that file to see which packages to analyze.

## IMPORTANT: Output location
Read the existing \`/guidelines/setup.md\` file first, then APPEND your findings below the existing content. Do NOT remove or modify the pre-written sections. Do NOT write any other files. Do NOT print the guidelines to chat \u{2014} write them as a file.

## What to document in \`/guidelines/setup.md\`

- **Install instructions**: the exact install instructions with all required packages (peer dependencies included).
- **Required CSS imports**: list every CSS file that must be imported and the recommended import order.
- **Provider / wrapper components**: if the design system requires a provider component at the app root, document it with all required props and show the recommended entry point pattern.
- **Build tool configuration**: any required Vite/Webpack/PostCSS/Tailwind configuration.
- **TypeScript**: any \`tsconfig.json\` requirements.
- **Peer dependencies**: list all peer dependencies and their version constraints.
- **Common gotchas**: things that silently break if misconfigured.

## Process

For each installed package, find and read the most informative files. Prioritize:

1. **README / CHANGELOG** \u{2014} setup instructions, provider requirements, and usage examples.
2. **package.json** \u{2014} check \`peerDependencies\`, \`exports\` (entry points), and \`style\`/\`css\` fields (required CSS imports).
3. **Type definitions** (\`.d.ts\` files) \u{2014} provider components, configuration types.
4. **CSS/SCSS source files** \u{2014} required CSS imports, theme files.

Do NOT rely on external documentation websites. Everything you need must come from what is shipped in the packages.

## Formatting rules

- Use Markdown for all output.
- Use fenced code blocks with language tags for all code examples.
- Keep the document concise but complete \u{2014} target 100-300 lines.
- Do not invent information. If a token or prop doesn't exist in the installed packages, omit it.
- Order content from most-used to least-used.`,te=["dependencies","devDependencies","peerDependencies"];var tt=r(100053),tr=r(291775),tn=r(439577),ta=r(33652);let ti=new Set(["dependencies","devDependencies","peerDependencies"]);function ts(e){try{let t=JSON.parse(e);return"object"==typeof t&&null!==t?t:null}catch{return null}}function tl(e){if(!e)return new Set;let t=[];for(let r of ti){let n=e[r];n&&"object"==typeof n&&t.push(...Object.keys(n))}return new Set(t)}async function to(e){let t={};for(let r of e.listFiles()){if(r.metadata.isHidden)continue;let e=await r.asyncContents;"string"==typeof e&&(t[r.path]=e)}return t}function td(e,t){let r=ts(e["/package.json"]??"{}"),n=ts(t["/package.json"]??"{}"),a=tl(r);return[...tl(n)].filter(e=>!a.has(e))}function tc(e,t){let r=function(e,t){if(!e&&!t)return"";if(!e)return"package.json was added";if(!t)return"package.json was deleted";let r=new Set([...Object.keys(e),...Object.keys(t)]),n=[];for(let a of r){if(ti.has(a))continue;let r=e[a],i=t[a],s=JSON.stringify(r),l=JSON.stringify(i);s!==l&&(void 0===r?n.push(`- Added \`${a}\`: ${l}`):void 0===i?n.push(`- Removed \`${a}\`: was ${s}`):n.push(`- Changed \`${a}\`: ${s} \u2192 ${l}`))}return n.join("\n")}(ts(e["/package.json"]??"{}"),ts(t["/package.json"]??"{}")),n=[];r&&n.push("The following package.json fields have been changed from the default template:\n"+r);let a=new Set([...Object.keys(e),...Object.keys(t)]),i=[];for(let r of a){if("/package.json"===r)continue;let n=e[r],a=t[r];if(n!==a){if(void 0===n&&void 0!==a){let e=a.split("\n").map(e=>`+ ${e}`);i.push(`[ADDED] ${r}
